desc:RON32 [summing] (GFX)
//tags: summing mixer unmasking separation clarity depth stems clean transient room
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-bypass, gfx-power and gfx-os (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// RON32 (Lab, an OG unit): RON32 with 32 channels - a summing mixer that listens to all sixteen stereo pairs at
// once and gives each
// one room by frequency, by time and by depth. Clean unless you engage TONE. Built from a user's wish (via JG,
// 28 Oct 2026) for summing with definition, separation and depth.
//
// SET-UP (REAPER): put RON32 on a bus track set to 32 channels (ROUTE > Track channels). Send each stem to its own
// pair (1/2, 3/4 ... 31/32) and turn off the stem tracks' master / parent send. The mix leaves on 1/2; outputs 3 - 32
// are silenced.
//
// SIGNAL FLOW: each pair -> MONO (optional) -> six gentle bells (110, 330, 990 Hz, 2.2, 5.5, 11 kHz: flat until needed)
//   -> BACK pairs: a little air off and softer attacks -> the sum -> TONE (LOW / HIGH lift, DIP 220 / 3K) -> MATCH ->
//   LEVEL TRIM. The detectors listen beside the audio; nothing in the audio path delays it.
//   BANK 1-16 / 17-32 (top bar): which eight pairs the strips and the ROOM MAP show (all sixteen are always heard
//                        and listened to; TAB in a name box runs on into the other bank).
//   PAIRS 1-2 .. 31-32   a NAME box (click, type, Enter; TAB = the next pair; saved with the project, shown under the ROOM MAP too);
//                        SIGNAL PRESENT LEDs; PLACE (one key, each click FRONT - MID - BACK, lit brightest at FRONT,
//                        dimmest at BACK; default MID): how much the pair
//                        matters (FRONT gives way last, BACK first) and, with DEPTH, how far back it sits; MONO.
//                        SOLO: hear only the soloed pairs, exactly as they sit in the mix (RON32 still listens to
//                        every pair, so you hear the room they were given); MUTE: the pair leaves the mix and the
//                        listening (the others get their room back). Both glide 10 ms; BYPASS follows them.
//                        NUDGE (- / +, 3 ms a click, -30 .. +30 ms; double-click or CTRL-click the readout = 0): moves
//                        the pair later (+) or earlier (-) against the others, to line up a stem's timing or a
//                        multi-miked source. RON32 listens to the pairs as nudged. A pair moved earlier means every
//                        other pair is delayed instead, so RON32 then reports that much latency (the most any pair is
//                        moved earlier); otherwise it stays at 0. A move crossfades 15 ms; a change of the latency
//                        dips 5 ms. BYPASS is the plain sum, without the nudges.
//   COPY GUARD           a pair that carries exactly what 1-2 carries (REAPER's pin connector feeding channels 1 / 2
//                        to every input, when RON32 went on a track before it had 32 channels) is left out of the
//                        listening and never moved; the strip and the ROOM MAP say so (the fix: the pin connector's
//                        Reset, with the track at 32 channels).
//   UNMASK (0 - 100 %)   in each of the six bands RON32 keeps a 900 ms RMS window of every pair (JG, 28 Oct 2026).
//                        Each pair's HOME band (where it is strongest against its own level, after a gentle tilt) is
//                        never cut. Where a pair is loud in a band another pair needs more (its home band, or a FRONT
//                        pair), the one that matters less dips there, by up to 4 dB at 100 % (usually 1 - 2 dB),
//                        never more than 3 dB of the pair's level in all. A pair playing alone is never touched.
//                        Cuts come in over about 30 ms and let go over about 150 ms, once the 900 ms window has
//                        moved on. FAST (JG, 29 Oct 2026: a square red lamp key under UNMASK): the decisions also
//                        hear an 80 ms ear, and cuts let go over 40 ms, so a clash that ends gives the band back
//                        within about a quarter of a second - more transparent on parts that come and go.
//   TRANSIENT (0 - 100 %) each pair's attacks (5 ms against 50 ms): when one pair hits, the other pairs dip briefly
//                        (up to 2.5 dB, following the attack) in the bands the hitting pair lives in, so the attack
//                        speaks first and the sustains fill in behind. A BACK pair can't push a FRONT one aside.
//   DEPTH (0 - 100 %)    BACK pairs only: up to -1.5 dB of air (a shelf from 8 kHz) and attacks rounded by up to
//                        2 dB. Tone and attack only - never a delay, so stems that share a source never comb.
//   FOCUS (MID .. WIDE, default the middle) where the room is made: at MID the pairs that give way give it only in
//                        the centre (the pair that matters comes through clear in the middle), at WIDE only at the
//                        sides (it opens out around it). A mono pair has no sides, so WIDE leaves it alone.
//   TONE (SIFON's COLOUR LOW / HIGH, JG 29 Oct 2026) on the whole mix, each key with its TEXTURE dial. RON32 is clean
//                        unless you engage TONE. LOW: a parallel saturation of the band below 300 Hz (tanh, biased:
//                        mostly 2nd harmonic) adding only its harmonics, driven 0 .. +18 dB by TEXTURE, plus a lift
//                        (to +1.25 dB, then from 50 % a 120 Hz lift to +2.3 dB and a 30 Hz subsonic filter). HIGH:
//                        the same on the top (from 3 kHz, reaching down to 1 kHz at 100 %), high-passed so the top
//                        gains sheen, plus a shelf from 4.7 kHz to +3.1 dB and from 50 % a 15 kHz shelf to +3 dB.
//                        DIP 220 (with LOW) / DIP 3K (with HIGH): a dip that cuts only while that region stands out
//                        from the whole mix (half the excess, up to 6 dB, 5 ms / 120 ms), and a fixed dip in the
//                        harmonics (-9 dB at 220 Hz / -6 dB at 3 kHz). With MATCH on, TONE's level is matched
//                        too (K-weighted, 3 s, -6 .. +1.5 dB): TONE changes the colour, not the level.
//   OS (1x / 2x / 4x, top bar, default 1x): TONE's saturation oversampled (the house half-bands); 2x = 31 samples of
//                        latency, 4x = 37 (reported; BYPASS and DELTA stay in time). Changing it dips 5 ms.
//   MATCH (default on)   RON32 only takes away, so it would come out slightly quieter: MATCH compares the result with
//                        the plain sum (K-weighted, 3 s) and makes up the difference (at most 1.5 dB), so BYPASS is
//                        a fair test of clarity, not of level.
//   DELTA                hear only what RON32 takes out (the plain sum minus the result). If DELTA sounds like music,
//                        it is working too hard.
//   ROOM MAP             six bands by the bank's eight pairs: each cell lights in its pair's colour with the pair's level in that
//                        band; the home band carries a bright mark; a cell that gives way dims, with its cut as a bar;
//                        a white flick is a transient dip.
//   OUTPUT METER         L / R LED ladders -42 .. +3 dBFS, peak hold 1.2 s, click to clear.
//   LEVEL TRIM           -3 .. +3 dB in 0.5 dB steps.
// OUTPUT: straight through (a mix tool: no clip). Every control at 0 (and MATCH either way) = the plain digital sum of
//   the 32 inputs, bit for bit.
// DRIFT: none (JG, 28 Oct 2026: no drift on any mastering or summing unit).
// MAINS (the ? pop-up, gfx-power; JG, 28 Oct 2026): MAINS OFF / UK / US (faint hum, sag, ripple) and EQUATOR
//   PROXIMITY (warm-up). Default OFF + NEAR = untouched. Nothing on the front panel but BYPASS.
// BYPASS (top bar, the house keycap): a 15 ms crossfade to the plain sum of the 32 inputs.
// PRESETS: the house preset bar. Presets set UNMASK and FAST, TRANSIENT, DEPTH, FOCUS, TONE, MATCH and TRIM, and leave the
//   PLACE, MONO and NUDGE keys and the names alone (they belong to the mix); "Reset all to defaults" (in the list) resets
//   everything but the names.
// GUI: drag a knob (SHIFT = fine, double-click or CTRL-click = default, wheel); click a key; click the LCD (or
//   PRESETS) for the preset list; click a name box to name the pair. Values show on hover. S / M / L / ? = size and help (+ MAINS).
// Latency: 0 samples (OS 2x: 31, 4x: 37; plus the most any pair is nudged earlier; reported). The in / out pins are declared, so REAPER carries any other track channels round it.

import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-bypass.jsfx-inc
import gfx-power.jsfx-inc
import gfx-os.jsfx-inc

